# Fix CAS2 Edge Case Test Failures - Systematic Implementation Plan

## Mission Overview

You are tasked with fixing **21 failing tests** out of 117 comprehensive CAS2 edge case tests. These tests were written following TDD principles and are currently failing because:
1. Some tests check for data we don't collect (need to remove these impossible tests)
2. Some require new module implementation (out-of-scope validator for data we DO have)
3. Some require logic enhancements (15m boundary handling)
4. Some have test data or assertion issues

**Revised Approach**: We only validate data we actually collect from users. Tests for non-existent fields (atriums, prisons, ICU, etc.) will be removed. Users will confirm their building has no complex features via a declaration checkbox.

Your approach must be **methodical, research-driven, and require human approval** before making any changes.

